1
00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:12,660
Let's get started. This time
we're actually going to

2
00:00:12,660 --> 00:00:16,300
dive into Linux networking.

3
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:18,340
We'll do this,
we'll ease into it

4
00:00:18,340 --> 00:00:21,500
with Linux network
device configuration,

5
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:25,410
and we're going to
use the IP link tool.

6
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:32,460
Our goal here is network
device configuration.

7
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:34,900
When we say device,
what do we mean?

8
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:38,300
There's all types of devices
that Linux supports.

9
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:42,140
This could refer to

10
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:46,810
physical interfaces
like Ethernet devices.

11
00:00:46,810 --> 00:00:49,420
It can refer to devices that

12
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:53,545
attach to another
device like a VLAN.

13
00:00:53,545 --> 00:00:55,825
They can connect together

14
00:00:55,825 --> 00:01:00,940
