19
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:20,695
a whole module dedicated to.

20
00:01:20,695 --> 00:01:25,580
But for now, let's get
into the IP link tool.

21
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:30,595
Now, as a little set the stage,

22
00:01:30,595 --> 00:01:33,040
there's different utilities that

23
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:36,580
could actually serve
the same purpose.

24
00:01:36,580 --> 00:01:39,860
We have one set of
utilities as part of

25
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:42,240
this iproute2 package and

26
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:45,320
then another set as
part of net-tools.

27
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:49,460
Iproute2 is a collection

28
00:01:49,460 --> 00:01:53,580
of utilities for controlling
TCP/IP networking,

29
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:56,225
and traffic control in Linux.

30
00:01:56,225 --> 00:01:58,400
Net-tools is a collection of

31
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:01,280
base networking
utilities for Linux,

32
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:03,030
like I have config,

33
00:02:03,030 --> 00:02:05,505
arp, route, and so forth.

34
00:02:05,505 --> 00:02:08,085
We'll use iproute2.

35
00:02:08,085 --> 00:02:10,280
But a lot of

36
00:02:10,280 --> 00:02:12,800
the things that you can
do that we'll talk about,

37
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:18,310
there's other tools and other
ways that you can do them.

38
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:24,380
We're going to focus in this
part right now on IP link.

39
00:02:24,380 --> 00:02:28,140
This is for network
device configuration

40
00:02:28,140 --> 00:02:32,275
for Linux and it's part
of this iproute2 package.

41
00:02:32,275 --> 00:02:36,675
The key commands are show,

42
